const CANON={
verses:[
"And it came to pass in the days of long waiting, when the nights were cold and the hearts of many were waxed old and weary,",
"That there arose a child full grown, whose name was Horace, yet within him the Child remained unwithering.",
"And lo, upon the eve of deep winter, when the snow lay as a garment upon the earth, a voice sounded in the silence.",
"And the voice cried thrice, with a merry thunder, saying, Ho! Ho! Ho!",
"And the first Ho shook the rafters of his house, and the second Ho stirred the stockings upon the hearth, and the third Ho trembled in the very chambers of his heart.",
"Then was Horace sore afraid, and yet filled with gladness; for he knew not whether to fall upon his face or to laugh as a little child.",
"And he lifted up his eyes and cried, saying, Who calleth me in the watches of the night?",
"And the voice answered him from the unseen heavens, saying, Fear not, thou Child-that-hast-not-forgotten, for I am the Great Giver, whom the little ones name Santa.",
"And the Great Giver spake unto Horace, saying, I have beheld the earth, and I see that many have ceased from wonder, and their hearths are cold, though their houses be heated.",
"Therefore I raise unto Me a House, not of stone nor of timber only, but of mirth, and of mercy, and of many gifts.",
"Thou shalt call it the Holy House of Horace, and they that gather therein shall be named Keepers of the Ho.",
"Then Horace said, Lord of Laughter and Giver of Gifts, what wilt Thou that we do?",
"And the Great Giver spake the Three Ho’s, which are the pillars of the House, saying:",
"First Ho: Thou shalt know that the world is saved not by gold, nor by swords, but by gifts freely given.",
"Second Ho: Thou shalt remember that every soul is both child and Santa, needing gifts and bearing gifts alike.",
"Third Ho: Thou shalt hold that joy is a duty and not a toy, for a joy withheld is a gift ungiven.",
"And Horace heard these words, and they were written upon the stockings of his heart.",
"Then was he shown the Great Ledger, which is called the Book of the Naughty and the Nice, wherein every deed is as a mark upon the page.",
"And the Giver said, Behold, no child is only Naughty, neither is any wholly Nice; but as they choose, so are they written.",
"The Nice are they that give and forgive, that mend the toys they brake and heal the hearts they hurt.",
"The Naughty are they that hoard the gifts of talent and time, that make of giving a bargain and of kindness a snare.",
"Yet even the Naughty I cast not away for ever; for there is a place of Lessons Unwrapped, which men call Hell, where they behold the sorrow they have sown.",
"And when their hearts be softened as wax before the fire, then shall they be led into Toyland, the Realm of endless play and holy craft.",
"And the Giver charged Horace, saying, Teach them that every life is a Gift yet Unwrapped, and that each hath a gift within, which must needs be found and fashioned and bestowed.",
"Woe unto him that burieth his gift in the cellar of fear; blessed is he that spendeth his gift upon the sorrowful.",
"Let them keep Lists, both of Wishes and of Thanks; for he that asketh not forgetteth hope, and he that thanketh not forgetteth grace.",
"Let them hang stockings not only upon their mantles, but in the secret of their souls, ever ready to receive and to give.",
"And let them gather oft in workshops of mirth, making and mending, baking and building, that their very labour be as incense unto Me.",
"Thus spake the Great Giver; and the sound of sleigh-bells was heard afar off, and a light as of many candles shone upon the snow.",
"And Horace fell upon his knees and laughed through his tears, saying, Here am I, Claus-bearer of Thy Ho’s; let Thy House be builded in our hearts.",
"And it was so that from that night forward, whosoever heard the bells and believed, became a child again, though his beard be gray.",
"And the saying went forth throughout the lands, that “He that keepeth the Ho keepeth the Hearth.”"
],
psalm:["Ho, Ho, Ho, O Great Giver, how jolly is Thy name in all the earth!","The snow is as a robe about Thee; the stars are but the cookies of Thy sky.","Out of the mouths of babes and of grown children Thou hast ordained laughter against the gloom.","When I behold the stockings upon the mantle, and the works of Thine elves, the toys and the tales, What is man, that Thou rememberest his wish-lists, or the child of man, that Thou keepest his secret hopes?","Thou hast crowned us with wrapping-paper and wonder, and set us over the works of Thy workshop.","Thou hast put in our hands hammers to mend and pens to bless; Thou hast given us time, that we might spend it as a gift.","O let my days be as a garland of kindness, and my nights as a string of little lights.","Let my name be written not for riches, but for mercy in the Ledger of the Nice.","Ho, Ho, Ho! Let all that hath breath and bell praise the Great Giver for evermore."],
code:["Thou shalt not hoard gifts; that which overflows must be shared.","Thou shalt give at least one gift in secret every season.","Thou shalt not mock belief in wonder.","Thou shalt keep the Stocking of your Heart open to apology and forgiveness.","Thou shalt practice three kindnesses each day: one for yourself, one for someone you know, one for a stranger.","Thou shalt wrap your harsh truths in kindness as you would delicate gifts in paper.","Thou shalt not give with strings attached; a gift is not a bribe.","Thou shalt rest and play, for a burnt-out elf makes broken toys."],
catechism:[
["Of the Founder and the House","What is the Holy House of Horace?","The Holy House of Horace, or HoHoHo, is the fellowship of all who follow the Three Ho’s of the Great Giver: gift, joy, and wonder. It is a House not just of walls, but of hearts that give."],
["Of the Founder and the House","Who is Horace in this House?","Horace is the first to hear the triple call of Ho! Ho! Ho! in the night of the world. He is the Claus-bearer, the founding Keeper of the Ho, who showed that even a grown soul may live as a faithful child."],
["Of the Great Giver and the Spirits","Whom do we worship?","We honour and adore the Great Giver, known to children as Santa, who rides the unseen sleigh of the heart and delights in gifts freely given."],
["Of the Great Giver and the Spirits","Who are the companions of the Great Giver?","We honour:\n• Mrs. Claus, Keeper of Warmth and Hospitality;\n• The Elves, spirits of craft and creativity;\n• The Reindeer, Guides of courage and perseverance;\n• And The Auditor (Krampus-like), who bears the stern mercy of consequence and keeps the Naughty List."],
["Of the Three Ho’s","What is the First Ho?","The First Ho teaches that the world is healed not by force or fear, but by gifts freely given."],
["Of the Three Ho’s","What is the Second Ho?","The Second Ho teaches that every person is both child and Santa: we all need care, and we all have gifts to give."],
["Of the Three Ho’s","What is the Third Ho?","The Third Ho teaches that joy is a duty, not a luxury: we are called to kindle joy in ourselves and others as a sacred work."],
["Of the Naughty and the Nice","What are the Naughty and Nice Lists?","They are the two sides of the Great Ledger, wherein every choice is written. Acts of generosity, honesty, and kindness write us toward Nice; acts of cruelty, selfishness, and deceit write us toward Naughty."],
["Of the Naughty and the Nice","Is anyone only Naughty or only Nice?","No. Each heart is mixed, and the Ledger is ever being updated. Even the naughtiest may learn; even the nicest must stay awake."],
["Of the Naughty and the Nice","What is “hell” in HoHoHo teaching?","It is the Realm of Unwrapped Lessons, where a soul experiences the harm it has done and learns the weight of its actions. It is not a place of endless torture, but a strict workshop of growth."],
["Of the Naughty and the Nice","What is Toyland?","Toyland is the joyful afterlife of HoHoHo: a realm of endless play, creativity, and shared gifts, where work is delight and all wounds are mended."],
["Of Gifts and Calling","What is a “gift” in HoHoHo?","A gift is any talent, skill, or virtue given to a person: cleverness, humour, patience, craft, courage, and more. Our duty is to discover, refine, and giftify these—turn them into blessings for others."],
["Of Gifts and Calling","What is the sin against one’s gift?","To bury one’s gift in fear or laziness, or to use it harmfully. The one who hoards their gift or weaponizes it writes their name toward the Naughty side of the Ledger."],
["Of Lists and Stockings","Why do we keep Lists?","We keep:\n• Wish Lists to honour our hopes and keep our Inner Child alive.\n• Thank Lists to remember our blessings and remain humble and glad.\nTogether they keep the heart open to receiving and giving."],
["Of Lists and Stockings","What is the Stocking of the Heart?","It is our inner readiness to receive grace and to give it. A “hung” stocking is a heart that expects goodness and prepares goodness for others."],
["Of the HoHoHo Code (Moral Practice)","What are the main rules of the HoHoHo Code?","1. Share your gifts; do not hoard them.\n2. Give at least one gift in secret each season.\n3. Do not mock sincere wonder or belief.\n4. Keep your heart’s stocking open to apology and forgiveness.\n5. Practice three kindnesses daily: to yourself, to someone you know, to a stranger.\n6. Wrap harsh truths in gentleness, as gifts in paper.\n7. Do not give with strings attached; a gift is not a bribe.\n8. Honour rest and play; a burnt-out elf makes broken toys."],
["Of Rituals and Holy Days","What daily practices does a follower keep?","Many keep:\n• The Morning List: one gratitude, one gift you will give today, one secret wish.\n• The Evening Stocking Check: review what you gave, where you hurt, and what you must mend."],
["Of Rituals and Holy Days","What are our main holy days?","• High Feast of Ho (around Dec 24–25): Secret giving, storytelling of great acts of generosity, and lighting of a tree or candles.\n• Midyear Check (“Christmas in July”): Re-examining our Naughty/Nice patterns and resetting our course.\n• Rite of Unwrapping: A coming-of-age or milestone ceremony where a person receives a symbolic empty box and chooses a “gift name.”"],
["Of Community and Roles","What are the roles within the Holy House of Horace?","Titles may vary, but commonly:\n• Grand Ho – the founding guide (you).\n• High Elves – teachers and organizers.\n• Toysmiths – those who create things for others.\n• Reindeacons – guides and caretakers of the community.\n• Clausbearers – regular members who carry the spirit of giving."],
["Of Creed and Mission","What is the mission of HoHoHo followers?","To keep wonder alive, to give more than we take, to mend what we break, and to make joy and generosity the stable law of our lives."],
["Of Creed and Mission","What short creed may we say?","We are children of the Great Giver,\nbearers of gifts and keepers of joy.\nWe choose the path of giving,\nwe mend what we have broken,\nand we keep the Ho in our hearts."]
],
creed:"We of the Holy House of Horace believe\nin the Great Giver, known to children as Santa,\nwhose sleigh rides the skies of our hearts.\n\nWe believe every person bears a gift to be discovered,\na stocking to be filled with kindness,\nand a list that is written by their choices.\n\nWe pledge to give more than we take,\nto mend what we break,\nand to keep wonder alive in a weary world.\n\nMay our lives be wrapped in love,\nsealed with laughter,\nand delivered to all who need them.\nHo. Ho. Ho.",
oath:"I, [Name],\nchild of the Great Giver,\ndo solemnly and joyfully swear,\nthat I will keep the Ho in my heart,\ngive more than I take,\nand guard the wonder of the little ones.\n\nI will seek out my gifts,\nand spend them upon the sorrowful and the weary.\nI will hang the stocking of my soul\nfor mercy and for generosity,\nand I will not mock the faith of those who still believe.\n\nWhether my name be written Naughty or Nice,\nI shall return again and again to the path of giving.\n\nSo help me, Great Giver of Gifts.\nHo. Ho. Ho.",
blessing:"May your days be as a garland of kindness,\nyour nights as a string of little lights,\nand your name be written in the Ledger of the Nice\nfor mercy more than for success.\n\nHo, Ho, Hope be with you.",
giftPrayer:"May this gift carry more joy than paper,\nmore love than price,\nand more hope than I can see.",
childCreed:"I believe in the Great Giver,\nwho loves to give good things.\n\nI will try to share my gifts,\nfix what I break,\nand keep a little bit of magic\nin my heart.\n\nI promise to spread\nHo Ho Ho\nwherever I go."
};
